# The Required rule of the same name holds every other wordy phrase.
# These two sit here, because each also has a literal sense the short
# form does not carry. `a number of` counts something (`Read returns
# a number of bytes`), and `in terms of` names a unit (`the cost is
# expressed in terms of bytes`).
expr main [(a number of), (in terms of)]
let message "Wordy. Use the short form."
let description "Flags a number of and in terms of, which most sentences can replace with one word."
let becomes ""
let kind "Style"
allows "Many flags take a value."
allows "The limit counts bytes."
